WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:08.870
I've got 27 BRAND NEW Things You Missed from
IT that you haven't seen in any of the other

00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:11.871
videos, so stick around to the end of this
one, where I'll reveal those.

00:00:11.871 --> 00:00:16.640
In the opening scene in Bill's room, you can
see a pad and pencils on his bed, a nod to

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:19.110
the fact that Bill grows up to become a writer
in the book.

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:23.279
If you look closer at the post where Patrick
Hockstetter's missing poster is displayed,

00:00:23.279 --> 00:00:26.590
you'll notice that it's absolutely covered
in staples.

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:30.570
Maybe not all of those staples are from missing
posters for children, but the number of staples

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:34.360
on that thing is pretty high, and at the end
of the movie we see a similar number of dead

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:36.990
kids floating in Pennywise's lair.

00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:40.941
So the staples really show us how many missing
children have just been given up on by the

00:00:40.941 --> 00:00:42.289
adults of Derry.

00:00:42.289 --> 00:00:47.359
What allows this to happen is described as
kind of a trance over all of the adults in

00:00:47.359 --> 00:00:48.359
Derry.

00:00:48.359 --> 00:00:52.339
Most of them seem to be in denial that there
really is a major problem with child abductions.

00:00:52.339 --> 00:00:56.460
Ben, as a newcomer to the town, noticed this
in his research.

00:00:56.460 --> 00:01:01.420
"Derry's not like any town I've ever been
in before.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:06.590
People die or disappear six times the national
average.

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:11.560
And that's just grown-ups.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:13.000
Kids are worse.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:14.000
WAY, way worse."

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.000
In another one of my videos, I discuss Belch's
T-shirt, and how it highlights the divide

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.000
between the child and adult perceptions of
what's going on in Derry.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:17.000
Roll the clip.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.130
"Belch is wearing an Anthrax shirt, which
is interesting because in the book, which

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:21.780
is set in the 50s rather than the 80s, one
of the few things that all the kids seems

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:27.000
to agree on, Lucky 7 and Bowers gang alike,
is their love for Rock &amp; Roll, a love that

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:30.780
is not shared with seemingly any of the adults
in Derry.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:35.939
That becomes kind a motif, a symbolic representation
of Pennywise's reign of terror in Derry.

00:01:35.939 --> 00:01:40.310
Adults are in denial and kind of turn a blind
eye to the reality of the situation because

00:01:40.310 --> 00:01:44.700
they're afraid of change, whether it be the
rise of Rock &amp; Roll in the 50s, or the rise

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.950
of an evil being in their town.

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:50.299
With this being set in the 80s, maybe metal
serves that purpose now."

00:01:50.299 --> 00:01:54.590
Belch also has an interesting shirt choice
during the rock fight.

00:01:54.590 --> 00:02:00.109
“Belch wears a T-shirt repping a demo CD
that Metallica put out in the 80s called Metal

00:02:00.109 --> 00:02:01.369
Up Your Ass.

00:02:01.369 --> 00:02:05.109
The graphic features a hand holding a sword
coming out of the toilet.

00:02:05.109 --> 00:02:10.710
Perfect choice for a movie about a dangerous
clown creature who also comes out of the sewers.”

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:14.610
That's not the only T-shirt in the movie that
seemed to be more than just a random choice

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:15.610
though.

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:17.300
There are a ctually many, many more.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:18.300
Starting with Eddie.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:22.470
He can be seen wearing this killer car shirt,
which is a reference to Stephen King's novel,

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:27.030
Christine about a vehicle that becomes possessed
and tries to kill its owner.

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:30.750
Bill wears a Tracker Bros. T-shirt when they
go to investigate the sewers.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:34.410
The Tracker Bros Shipping Company is a family
owned trucking service from the book.

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:39.190
They don't come up in the movie, so this is
just a cool little easter egg.

00:02:39.190 --> 00:02:43.000
T-shirts were not the only thing in the art
department that have significance.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:44.450
Let's roll that next clip.

00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:49.520
"Bill has some posters in his room, and I
was able to identify a couple of them as Gremlins

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:51.050
and Beetlejuice.

00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:52.220
Why is this significant?

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:55.440
Well, I think these posters both have double
meanings behind them.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:58.000
The first is a foreshadowing of Bill's future.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:02.271
You'll find that after facing their fears
in the movie, that none of the 'losers' are

00:03:02.271 --> 00:03:03.370
losers anymore.

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:06.570
They all go on to have very successful careers.

00:03:06.570 --> 00:03:10.160
Perhaps the most successful of them though,
is Bill Denborough.

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:12.530
Who grows up to be a horror writer.

00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:14.260
Like me.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:15.770
But without the stupid goatee.

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:19.460
But it's cool to see that Bill does have an
interest in horror as a kid, and that leads

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:21.630
into his occupation as an adult.

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:25.570
On a side note, pretty much every Stephen
King novel has a protagonist who's a writer,

00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:29.040
a method he uses to project himself into his
work.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:33.100
Muschietti and his art department could have
chosen any two horror movie posters to hang

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:35.850
on Bill's wall though, so why did they choose
these?"

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:40.320
I mean... outside the fact that they are both
Warner Bros movies and they would never market

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.380
for a competitor?

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:44.700
Go on, me from a month ago.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:50.040
"Bill's still a kid, and these are both more
kid-friendly horror movies that came out in

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:51.220
the 1980s.

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:55.440
But I think there's a reason that these were
chosen as opposed to say...

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:56.630
Ghostbusters.

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:57.800
Let's look at Gremlins.

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:03.010
It's a movie about these little things that
change into other, more scary things, and

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:07.380
in this movie, IT's shapeshifting abilities
are on full display, one of which being the

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:12.130
transformation that IT does with it's teeth
when feeding off the fear of the children.

00:04:12.130 --> 00:04:16.930
It seemed like it took some big inspiration
from Barbara's transformation in Beetlejuice.

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:22.169
How the face kind of peels back to reveal
these rows and rows of razor sharp teeth.

00:04:22.169 --> 00:04:25.610
Especially that scene where Pennywise is about
to feed on Stan.

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:28.800
I was getting major vibes from the Tim Burton
classic."

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:33.680
It seems that there was also some inspiration
from more traditional circus clowns like Georgie’s

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:38.870
wallpaper and the overall decor in his room,
from stuffed animals to little dolls on the

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:39.870
nightstand.

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:43.740
One of my favorite parts about the movie is
how there is always something looming in the

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:48.551
dark, so in this next clip, I'll talk about
what lies beyond the light.

00:04:48.551 --> 00:04:52.539
"The whole basement scene is pretty dark in
this shot, so let's turn up the lights.

00:04:52.539 --> 00:04:55.980
In the corner, there are some oars, and there's
also a life vest on the wall.

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:59.849
I wonder if these choices have anything to
do with the fact that Georgie dies while playing

00:04:59.849 --> 00:05:00.920
with the paper boat."

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:05.560
Note: this does make sense, because this is
right before Pennywise uses Georgie's image

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:07.139
to try to trick Bill.

00:05:07.139 --> 00:05:09.039
"OK, this is creepy.

00:05:09.039 --> 00:05:11.699
First thing I noticed in Pennywise sinking
into the well.

00:05:11.699 --> 00:05:16.580
If Ringu didn't make wells creepy enough for
you, it looks like the clown's got you covered.

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:19.639
Scattered on the floor are children's clothes
and toys.

00:05:19.639 --> 00:05:22.849
This looks like of like an elephant, another
circus animal.

00:05:22.849 --> 00:05:24.870
There's also a noose hanging from the rafter.

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:28.400
This room is full of various clowns and has
a few things that I loved.

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:30.689
I'll turn up the lights again to make it easier
for you to see.

00:05:30.689 --> 00:05:34.599
This little guy right here is a nice throwback
to the Tim Curry Pennywise design from the

00:05:34.599 --> 00:05:36.740
1990 TV mini-series."

00:05:36.740 --> 00:05:40.729
This clown's head turns to follow Richie as
he walks.

00:05:40.729 --> 00:05:45.259
It's good to see something subtle like that
and know that it's not all just jump scares.

00:05:45.259 --> 00:05:48.621
When they align the map of Derry with the
sewer system map, we discover that the sewer

00:05:48.621 --> 00:05:53.430
lines run through the 29 Neibolt House and
the kids make a plan to go confront Pennywise

00:05:53.430 --> 00:05:54.430
there.

00:05:54.430 --> 00:05:58.060
If you look at some of the other locations
on that map, you'll also see the cemetery,

00:05:58.060 --> 00:06:02.699
which means we will probably see Bill's confrontation
with Pennywise in the sequel, where Pennywise

00:06:02.699 --> 00:06:05.220
is digging graves for each of the Lucky 7.

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:08.289
The references are far from being over there
though.

00:06:08.289 --> 00:06:12.740
“During the beginning of the film you may
have heard Bill uttering the following phrase:

00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:17.930
‘he thrusts his fists against the posts
and still insists he sees the ghosts.’

00:06:17.930 --> 00:06:20.220
It comes back at the end of the film I believe.

00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:24.599
What this is is a coping mechanism to help
Bill with his stutter and it’s something

00:06:24.599 --> 00:06:28.940
that helps him overcome Pennywise in the book
because his stutter is directly linked to

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:30.129
his fear of IT.

00:06:30.129 --> 00:06:35.400
It’s not that bad at first but it gets worse
when Georgie is killed and when his fear of

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:38.509
IT increases, the stutter gets worse.

00:06:38.509 --> 00:06:42.389
Remember when he has the courage to go into
the 29 Neibolt house after they discover that

00:06:42.389 --> 00:06:45.180
it’s connected to the old wellhouse and
it’s connected to the sewer?

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:49.590
He gives his friends a speech and Richie even
comments on him having not stuttered through

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:50.590
any of it.

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:53.159
That’s his courage that allows him to stand
up like that.

00:06:53.159 --> 00:06:56.729
So when you hear him say the phrase ‘he
thrusts his fists against the posts and still

00:06:56.729 --> 00:07:01.250
insists he sees the ghosts,’ without stuttering,
you know that he has grown in the face of

00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:04.999
fear in order to do so, and that’s what
weakens IT.

00:07:04.999 --> 00:07:09.409
I would expect to hear more of that phrase
when his childhood stutter comes back in Chapter

00:07:09.409 --> 00:07:10.430
2.

00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:14.249
There were a lot of little nods to events
and characters in the book that were touched

00:07:14.249 --> 00:07:17.759
on in the movie but didn’t need to be fully
expanded.

00:07:17.759 --> 00:07:21.389
Some of these things had their own chapter
in the book, but I think the film did a nice

00:07:21.389 --> 00:07:25.020
job of only including what was necessary as
not to overwhelm the viewer.

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:27.449
Here are a few of those references.

00:07:27.449 --> 00:07:32.810
Ben researches the ironworks explosion, a
catastrophe caused by IT in the early 1900s.

00:07:32.810 --> 00:07:38.909
He also looks up the Black Spot fire, which
was a nightclub in Derry during the early

00:07:38.909 --> 00:07:43.240
1930s that was a hangout for a lot of African-American
men at the time.

00:07:43.240 --> 00:07:48.340
It was burned down by a racist faction with
only a few survivors, one of which being Mike

00:07:48.340 --> 00:07:51.570
Hanlon’s dad, who passes the story onto
his son.

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:56.539
The relevancy of that in this movie is debatable,
because Mike’s parents actually do die in

00:07:56.539 --> 00:07:58.750
a fire prior to the events of 1989.”

00:07:58.750 --> 00:08:02.370
(Inside missing poster) Throughout the entire
movie, the town is covered in missing posters

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:04.210
for the abducted children.

00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:08.059
Many of these are references to characters
in the book whom we never meet in the movie,

00:08:08.059 --> 00:08:10.800
at least not when they are alive.

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:11.800
Betty Ripson and

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:13.669
Edward Corcoran are a couple of examples.

00:08:13.669 --> 00:08:18.509
I found a lot of elements from the book that
were in the movie but not really explained.

00:08:18.509 --> 00:08:19.509
Check this out.

00:08:19.509 --> 00:08:24.360
“At one point Pennywise encounters Richie
and uses the line Beep-Beep Richie, which

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:29.139
is a phrase the Lucky 7 always uses in the
book whenever Richie doesn’t shut up.

00:08:29.139 --> 00:08:33.460
It doesn’t come up a whole lot in the movie,
but Richie does still run his mouth a lot.

00:08:33.460 --> 00:08:37.190
The reason I wanted to bring it up, was that
I think it kind of takes on a new meaning

00:08:37.190 --> 00:08:40.910
here with how much of a pottymouth Richie
is in this movie.

00:08:40.910 --> 00:08:44.630
The beep-beep could represent the redacted
expletives.

00:08:44.630 --> 00:08:46.220
One other note on Richie.

00:08:46.220 --> 00:08:51.160
At the school when Richie walks by the gang
of bullies, Patrick Hockstetter (the one who

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:55.730
goes after them with a makeshift flamethrower,
gives him this creepy smile and licks his

00:08:55.730 --> 00:08:57.600
lips.

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:00.840
One thing this movie was very good at is telling
a lot of backstory visually.

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:07.440
Patrick is one messed up kid who gets off
on hurting other and has weird violent-homosexual

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:08.440
tendencies.

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:12.970
At one point in the book he actually molests
Henry Bowers, lwhich is why I think he’s

00:09:12.970 --> 00:09:14.910
actually the scariest human character.

00:09:14.910 --> 00:09:18.950
He doesn’t get that far in the movie, but
that little lick of the lips at a boy who

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:24.600
is substantially younger than him tells us
that something is not right about his character.

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:28.080
There were a couple of things that were different
from the book, but I think actually added

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:30.170
to some of the character arcs in the movie.

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:35.501
For example, while Stan is Jewish in both
the novel and motion picture, his religion

00:09:35.501 --> 00:09:37.760
plays a much bigger part now.

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:41.260
Stan is studying for his bar-mitzvah, and
his father is the rabbi of the temple.

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:45.750
But we’re given the idea that Stan isn’t
really a big believer because he hasn’t

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:47.600
been studying his Torah portion.

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:51.240
In fact, the blessing that he’s having trouble
with is actually just the prayer you have

00:09:51.240 --> 00:09:55.670
to recite before opening the Torah, so it’s
like the easiest one because it always comes

00:09:55.670 --> 00:09:57.870
up, but he can’t even get through that.

00:09:57.870 --> 00:10:02.310
The reason I think this is kind of a brilliant
change from the book, is that the whole basis

00:10:02.310 --> 00:10:06.740
of Stan’s character is that he’s the last
one to truly believe in IT.

00:10:06.740 --> 00:10:12.330
He even says that the things that they’re
all seeing aren’t real… until the Neibolt

00:10:12.330 --> 00:10:16.270
House encounter, and it hits him the hardest
it.

00:10:16.270 --> 00:10:21.210
Once he believes in IT, he’s probably the
most scared of IT, and right after that happens

00:10:21.210 --> 00:10:25.000
we’re led into the montage of the middle
of that summer, where he actually has his

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:26.120
bar-mitzvah.

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:29.600
His belief in IT mirrors his faith in his
religion.”

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:33.750
There were even a couple of Things You Missed
that added a touch of metacinema.

00:10:33.750 --> 00:10:37.930
In the projector scene, there are a couple
of inserts of slides being put into the projector.

00:10:37.930 --> 00:10:42.200
One says Made in Canada, and one says Made
in USA.

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:45.860
Filming locations for this movie swapped back
and forth between these two countries, with

00:10:45.860 --> 00:10:49.790
much of Derry taking place in the Canadian
city Port Hope, Ontario.

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:53.180
One thing that might have gone over your head
is the significance behind the release date:

00:10:53.180 --> 00:10:54.180
September 8, 2016.

00:10:54.180 --> 00:10:56.420
I discussed this in detail in a previous video.

00:10:56.420 --> 00:11:00.560
Roll it: "What's more interesting to me is
WHY the filmmakers have chose the 80s for

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:01.560
this film.

00:11:01.560 --> 00:11:04.981
Many of you confirmed my suspicion that the
book will be split into two movies, meaning

00:11:04.981 --> 00:11:10.800
that the second movie will take place in 2016;
the same year that Part 1 was in production.

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:14.350
When you consider the fact that the first
movie is technically a flashback, that kind

00:11:14.350 --> 00:11:18.930
of makes this whole reboot series a modern
day remake of IT, an interesting choice when

00:11:18.930 --> 00:11:23.620
you consider the significance of creepy clowns
in our culture today such as the Staten Island

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:26.930
Clown and his many copycats over the last
few years.

00:11:26.930 --> 00:11:29.300
We'll see if that plays into the second film
at all.

00:11:29.300 --> 00:11:33.170
I'll never forget that scene in the adult
portion of the miniseries where Ben notices

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:37.140
Pennywise on the side of the road, something
that seemed to happen quite a lot in America

00:11:37.140 --> 00:11:39.740
in October 2016.

00:11:39.740 --> 00:11:40.930
This is our next item.

00:11:40.930 --> 00:11:43.880
The film is scheduled to release September
8th, 2017.

00:11:43.880 --> 00:11:47.080
You might be wondering, 'CZ, how did you miss
this?

00:11:47.080 --> 00:11:48.320
It says it right there.'

00:11:48.320 --> 00:11:53.120
Well it's not the release date I missed, but
rather, the significance behind it.

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:58.330
In the story, IT returns to the town every
27 years to terrorize Derry.

00:11:58.330 --> 00:12:03.000
Commenter CynicalCatLady points out, 'The
first screen adaptation of IT was first aired

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:09.690
in 1990, and 27 years later the infamous dancing
clown is re-emerging to breath fresh terror

00:12:09.690 --> 00:12:13.490
into a new generation, just as he does in
the novel.'”

00:12:13.490 --> 00:12:16.900
If you haven’t read the book, be warned.

00:12:16.900 --> 00:12:21.300
We’re going into spoiler territory.

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:23.320
Welcome to spoiler territory.

00:12:23.320 --> 00:12:26.740
In the scene where Georgie is playing with
the boat, you'll notice tents bolstered with

00:12:26.740 --> 00:12:32.390
sandbags all around street covering up the
sewage caps to prevent the sewer access areas

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:34.070
from being flooded.

00:12:34.070 --> 00:12:39.490
This plant the seed early that Derry is set
up in a way that might be prone to flooding,

00:12:39.490 --> 00:12:44.950
so don't be surprised if there is a massive
flood at the end of IT: Chapter 2.

00:12:44.950 --> 00:12:49.501
There are a number of subtle references to
astronomy throughout the movie, which foreshadow

00:12:49.501 --> 00:12:53.640
the possible inclusion of the Macroverse in
the sequel.

00:12:53.640 --> 00:12:56.980
The macroverse is a dark void that surrounds
our own universe.

00:12:56.980 --> 00:13:02.790
It is the place from which IT and the natural
enemy of IT, known as The Turtle, originate

00:13:02.790 --> 00:13:03.790
from.

00:13:03.790 --> 00:13:07.921
The only way they are able to defeat IT in
the book involves a ceremony known as the

00:13:07.921 --> 00:13:12.890
Ritual of Chud, where... and stay with me
here...

00:13:12.890 --> 00:13:18.050
Bill's consciousness transcends his actual
body and our universe and has a psychic showdown

00:13:18.050 --> 00:13:23.780
with it in the Macroverse where he is given
the power to defeat IT by The Turtle.

00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:28.440
So because of these deep ties to Macroverse,
we see countless astronomical references scattered

00:13:28.440 --> 00:13:29.910
throughout Derry.

00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:33.020
Bill has a solar system model above his desk,

00:13:33.020 --> 00:13:35.330
a rocket ship on his desk,

00:13:35.330 --> 00:13:40.010
and a globe next to his desk, signifying that
he could be the one to travel to the macroverse,

00:13:40.010 --> 00:13:42.070
which we'll likely see in chapter 2.

00:13:42.070 --> 00:13:46.800
When they are in Bill's garage, Ben has a
T-shirt with many solar systems on it.

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:52.150
The Derry library shows another globe, representing
earth, looking very insignificant

00:13:52.150 --> 00:13:57.120
across from a poster that represents the scale
of the greater universe; it says reach for

00:13:57.120 --> 00:13:59.040
the stars, read a book.

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:02.950
---In addition to the broader space references,
there are also some references to The Turtle

00:14:02.950 --> 00:14:03.950
itself.

00:14:03.950 --> 00:14:05.130
Check out the clip where I talk about that:
“The other thing I noticed was the lego

00:14:05.130 --> 00:14:09.170
turtle that Bill finds in his brother’s
old room, which was one of the few references

00:14:09.170 --> 00:14:13.820
to a celestial being known as The Turtle,
who is an opposing force against IT.

00:14:13.820 --> 00:14:17.380
The turtle is kind of slyly written into the
book.

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:21.250
Characters will find themselves thinking about
The Turtle without really knowing why.

00:14:21.250 --> 00:14:24.970
In the movie, one of the characters brings
up the fact that they think they see a Turtle

00:14:24.970 --> 00:14:26.700
in the swimming scene,

00:14:26.700 --> 00:14:30.620
and I’m not entirely sure, because again,
I can’t pause yet, but I’m pretty sure

00:14:30.620 --> 00:14:33.910
I saw a turtle sticker on one of Beverly’s
books.

00:14:33.910 --> 00:14:37.490
These references are nothing more than Easter
Eggs though, because the primary scene in

00:14:37.490 --> 00:14:42.800
which The Turtle gives advice to Bill known
as The Ritual of Chud, is not a scene in this

00:14:42.800 --> 00:14:43.800
movie.”

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:45.160
I wouldn’t rule it out for the sequel though.

00:14:45.160 --> 00:14:49.640
“The Turtle’s rival, who the kids refer
to as IT, but whose true form is known as

00:14:49.640 --> 00:14:54.780
The Deadlights does make a brief appearance
when Pennywise tries to eat Beverly and it’s

00:14:54.780 --> 00:14:58.780
face peels back, she looks down it’s throat
and sees three bright lights.

00:14:58.780 --> 00:15:02.510
This is somewhat different than the form we’re
used to seeing The Deadlights in.

00:15:02.510 --> 00:15:07.700
They appear to be more of a force within Pennywise,
as opposed to their own powerful entity.

00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:11.970
Nobody in the movie ever uses the word ‘Deadlights’
so they make their way onto the silver screen

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:13.760
in a much more subtle way.

00:15:13.760 --> 00:15:17.430
This next one I didn’t notice until the
last scene of the movie.

00:15:17.430 --> 00:15:21.270
In a previous Things You Missed, I pointed
out that Beverly wears a key around her neck,

00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:23.590
and speculated what it might be for.

00:15:23.590 --> 00:15:29.950
Many, and I mean a lot, like 666 billion of
you pointed out that the key is uncut, so

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:32.510
it couldn’t actually be used for unlocking
anything.

00:15:32.510 --> 00:15:36.800
After seeing the movie, I still have no idea
what the significance of the key is, but I

00:15:36.800 --> 00:15:39.380
noticed another piece of Jewelry that Bev
has.

00:15:39.380 --> 00:15:41.650
It’s a ring with an anchor on it.

00:15:41.650 --> 00:15:43.070
What do anchors do?

00:15:43.070 --> 00:15:44.130
They sink.

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:48.270
And after countless cases of ‘you’ll float
too’, ‘you’ll float too’, ‘YOU’LL

00:15:48.270 --> 00:15:53.460
FLOAT TOO’, the group eventually finds that
Beverly floats as well, after being abducted

00:15:53.460 --> 00:15:54.470
by Pennywise.

00:15:54.470 --> 00:15:58.890
But because of the love and dedication of
her friends, they’re able to find her and

00:15:58.890 --> 00:16:01.330
pull her back down out of harm’s way.

00:16:01.330 --> 00:16:07.590
In a world where all of the victims float,
she’s the one who sinks, she’s the anchor.

00:16:07.590 --> 00:16:11.800
In that final scene, after the promise, Bev
tells what she remembers from when she was

00:16:11.800 --> 00:16:16.550
afloat and says she had a vision of them from
when they are all much older in their 30s

00:16:16.550 --> 00:16:22.870
this is a foreshadowing of the sequel, when
after a 27 year rest, Pennywise re-emerges

00:16:22.870 --> 00:16:27.760
and the losers are called back to Derry to
fulfill their promise and vanquish IT.”

00:16:27.760 --> 00:16:32.380
There was also a Stephen King movie called
The Dark Tower that came out earlier in the

00:16:32.380 --> 00:16:36.390
year, and many of you speculated that there
might be some kind of Stephen King cinematic

00:16:36.390 --> 00:16:41.110
universe in the works, despite the fact that
the movies are made by different studios.

00:16:41.110 --> 00:16:45.000
After seeing both movies, that doesn't appear
to be the case, but it's still hard not to

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:49.000
notice some references to Stephen King lore
throughout the film.

00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:53.830
And before I roll this clip, I'd like to mention
that this whole idea was brought about by

00:16:53.830 --> 00:16:59.690
THIS teaser for The Dark Tower, featuring
The Shining, IT, Carrie, The Shawshank Redemption,

00:16:59.690 --> 00:17:01.810
Christine and The Stand.

00:17:01.810 --> 00:17:02.810
Let's roll it.

00:17:02.810 --> 00:17:04.740
"Smith Coronna is a typewriter company.

00:17:04.740 --> 00:17:07.500
The typewriter is a very important prop in
The Shining.

00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:11.379
I already mentioned the Christine shirt, and
there's this newspaper headline that says

00:17:11.379 --> 00:17:15.879
'NO INDICTMENT YET ON GILLESPIE.' and I wasn't
able to read anything past that, but Gillespie

00:17:15.879 --> 00:17:19.159
is a character in Salem's Lot, in fact, he's
a cop.

00:17:19.159 --> 00:17:24.980
By the way, did this shot kind of remind anyone
of Salem's Lot?"

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:28.400
After seeing The Dark Tower, I think it's
also worth noting that when Roland describes

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:33.710
The Macroverse to Jake while they are camping
out at the abandoned Pennywise amusement park,

00:17:33.710 --> 00:17:37.759
he draws a circle in the sand to represent
their universe, and talks about how higher

00:17:37.759 --> 00:17:42.620
beings can travel from the outer Macroverse
into their universe, and to represent this,

00:17:42.620 --> 00:17:47.340
a tarantula crawls across the sand on his
diagram, which of course reminded me of the

00:17:47.340 --> 00:17:53.919
final form ["This isn't even my final form!"]
of IT, or at least the final form shown in

00:17:53.919 --> 00:17:56.669
the book which is a giant spider.

00:17:56.669 --> 00:18:00.429
So that covers all of the Things You Missed
from past videos that are still relevant now

00:18:00.429 --> 00:18:05.010
that the movie has been released, and it's
a great spot to transition into the new Things

00:18:05.010 --> 00:18:09.620
You Missed that have never been mentioned
before, the first of which being an allusion

00:18:09.620 --> 00:18:11.919
to the spider that I just brought up.

00:18:11.919 --> 00:18:16.120
During the final battle with Pennywise, when
he's going all ditto on the losers, one of

00:18:16.120 --> 00:18:20.200
the forms he takes looks like an arachnid,
at first I thought it looked more like a praying

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:25.470
mantis than anything, and I'll stand by that,
but some of you said it reminded you of the

00:18:25.470 --> 00:18:30.240
spider, and after seeing the mini-series again,
where they banquish Pennywise as kids and

00:18:30.240 --> 00:18:34.970
IT's arm turns into a spider for just a second
before retreating deeper into the sewers,

00:18:34.970 --> 00:18:37.460
I can kind of see the resemblance.

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:41.340
When Georgie goes into the basement to get
the wax, they have a clothesline with stuff

00:18:41.340 --> 00:18:46.000
drying on it even though they seem to have
a washer and dryer already, so the clothesline

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:50.150
must be another throwback to the mini-series
where Pennywise hides behind sheets on the

00:18:50.150 --> 00:18:52.419
clothesline to get Laurie-Ann.

00:18:52.419 --> 00:18:56.249
Also when Georgie is down in the basement,
he sees a couple of lights which he perceives

00:18:56.249 --> 00:19:01.590
as eyes, but we later find out that they kind
of resemble the deadlights that Beverly sees

00:19:01.590 --> 00:19:03.379
inside of Pennywise.

00:19:03.379 --> 00:19:08.370
When Bill builds the boat for his brother,
Georgie refers to the craft as "it".

00:19:08.370 --> 00:19:11.960
Bill corrects him, telling him he should always
call a boat she.

00:19:11.960 --> 00:19:15.950
This line goes nicely with what I brought
up earlier about Beverly being the anchor

00:19:15.950 --> 00:19:17.059
of the group.

00:19:17.059 --> 00:19:20.730
Also, remember Belch's Anthrax shirt I brought
up before?

00:19:20.730 --> 00:19:23.830
I noticed that it has text on the back as
well.

00:19:23.830 --> 00:19:29.130
It says "follow me or die", which fits in
with Belch's character because he just kind

00:19:29.130 --> 00:19:31.799
of blindly follows Henry Bowers out of fear.

00:19:31.799 --> 00:19:35.750
It's also clear that he isn't comfortable
with how Henry is cutting Ben's stomach, but

00:19:35.750 --> 00:19:36.820
he won't stand up to Henry.

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:42.070
I also have a theory that Belch does die in
this movie, but I'll get back to that in a

00:19:42.070 --> 00:19:43.070
bit.

00:19:43.070 --> 00:19:46.009
Some people were pointing out that the lady
from the painting creature that Stan is afraid

00:19:46.009 --> 00:19:52.570
of resembles Mama, from the 2013 movie Mama,
also directed by Andy Muschietti.

00:19:52.570 --> 00:19:57.670
I wouldn't go so far as to say that it's the
same creature, but I can see a slight resemblance.

00:19:57.670 --> 00:20:02.580
We see a couple of hero shots of Bill's bike,
which he has named Silver, and in one scene,

00:20:02.580 --> 00:20:06.700
while Ben is in the library, Bill and the
others are riding bikes in the street and

00:20:06.700 --> 00:20:11.149
he hear the signature phrase, "Hi, ho Silver,
away," which is a reference to the Lone Ranger,

00:20:11.149 --> 00:20:16.100
but more importantly, a phrase that Bill imitates
in the book on several occasions when his

00:20:16.100 --> 00:20:18.119
speedy bike-riding saves the day.

00:20:18.119 --> 00:20:22.840
As Ben is researching in the library, he looks
at a photo from April 3rd, 1908, which is

00:20:22.840 --> 00:20:26.820
when the Iron Works explosion was, and Pennywise
can be seen hiding in the photo.

00:20:26.820 --> 00:20:30.350
I don't have a still for this, so you'll have
to go see for yourself.

00:20:30.350 --> 00:20:33.929
We don't find out a whole lot about Beverly's
father in this movie, but he does wear a shirt

00:20:33.929 --> 00:20:35.710
and hat that say "Maintenence".

00:20:35.710 --> 00:20:40.520
Originally, Bev's Dad is the school janitor,
so that could explain why he's privy to the

00:20:40.520 --> 00:20:42.450
rumors that go around about her.

00:20:42.450 --> 00:20:47.720
One of the books in Bev's room is The Frog
Prince, which foreshadows the idea of a kiss

00:20:47.720 --> 00:20:51.389
being what brings her back in the end when
Ben’s kiss snaps her out of her trance or

00:20:51.389 --> 00:20:53.559
whatever it is that Pennywise has done to
her.

00:20:53.559 --> 00:20:58.110
I caught a few more astronomical nods to add
to the ones I listed before.

00:20:58.110 --> 00:21:02.710
In Ben's room, he has rather large posters
of the the Earth and the Moon, in addition

00:21:02.710 --> 00:21:03.710
to another globe.

00:21:03.710 --> 00:21:07.850
A towel on the back of Bev's door appears
to have some space patterns.

00:21:07.850 --> 00:21:11.740
There is also a picture of a flying saucer
above Georgie's bed.

00:21:11.740 --> 00:21:16.840
And when they first go into the 29 Neibolt
house, Stan has a small icon of the sun on

00:21:16.840 --> 00:21:18.240
his shirt.

00:21:18.240 --> 00:21:21.590
And while we're bringing up shirts, some of
you wanted me to look into Richie's shirt

00:21:21.590 --> 00:21:23.919
that reps: 'Freese's Department Store'.

00:21:23.919 --> 00:21:28.990
I guess this was a real life store in the
actual town in Maine that inspired Stephen

00:21:28.990 --> 00:21:30.519
King to write Derry.

00:21:30.519 --> 00:21:35.649
Beverly has a poster in her room for the punk
band Siouxsie and the Banshees.

00:21:35.649 --> 00:21:40.110
Beverly herself is like a frontwoman in a
band of all boys in the losers club.

00:21:40.110 --> 00:21:44.179
When the kids go down into the sewer, everything
and everyone that went down the drain over

00:21:44.179 --> 00:21:48.840
the course of the film can be found, including
Beverly's hair which is seen dripping out

00:21:48.840 --> 00:21:50.090
of a pipe.

00:21:50.090 --> 00:21:54.049
After defeating Pennywise, the group shares
a hug, but if you look in the background there

00:21:54.049 --> 00:21:59.850
is a light being emitted from the drain that
Pennywise retreated into -- this is IT retaking

00:21:59.850 --> 00:22:03.490
it's true form as The Deadlights.

00:22:03.490 --> 00:22:08.150
All of the abusive parents in the town are
seen watching the same TV show, which appears

00:22:08.150 --> 00:22:12.490
to be a children's show that encourages kids
to go down into the sewers and give themselves

00:22:12.490 --> 00:22:13.879
up to Pennywise.

00:22:13.879 --> 00:22:18.850
First, Eddie's mom is seen watching it and
we just get a small glimpse.

00:22:18.850 --> 00:22:23.450
Next we find Bev's dad watching the program
and hear the line "When you follow your friends

00:22:23.450 --> 00:22:26.379
in the sewers, you can be with clowns!"

00:22:26.379 --> 00:22:28.950
So that's pretty disturbing.

00:22:28.950 --> 00:22:33.879
But then the show is on in front of Henry's
dad who is asleep on the couch near the end.

00:22:33.879 --> 00:22:38.360
Pennywise appears and encourages Henry to
kill his father, and then 'kill them all'

00:22:38.360 --> 00:22:40.330
in a frenzied chant.

00:22:40.330 --> 00:22:45.250
Maybe this show is what brainwashes the adults
-- the reason that they all seem so oblivious

00:22:45.250 --> 00:22:49.929
to IT, the reason Bev’s dad can’t see
the blood and the reason Eddie’s Mom won’t

00:22:49.929 --> 00:22:53.110
look past the fact that the pills are only
gazebos…

00:22:53.110 --> 00:22:55.269
I mean placebos.

00:22:55.269 --> 00:22:59.269
This show was also on the TV when I walked
through the Neibolt House Hollywood, so I

00:22:59.269 --> 00:23:01.320
got to catch a little bit more of it.

00:23:01.320 --> 00:23:14.030
I'll roll that clip for you.

00:23:14.030 --> 00:23:25.330
[Clip]

00:23:25.330 --> 00:23:29.059
If you want to see that whole walkthrough,
I'll leave a link to my video in the card

00:23:29.059 --> 00:23:30.139
right here.

00:23:30.139 --> 00:23:36.409
Incidentally, I think Henry does end up "killing
them all," or at least he tries.

00:23:36.409 --> 00:23:41.130
When he shows up to ambush the Losers at the
29 Neibolt House just before the film’s

00:23:41.130 --> 00:23:48.159
end, he rolls up in Belch's car, the Trans
Am, with considerably more blood on his face

00:23:48.159 --> 00:23:51.090
than when we last saw him when he killed his
Dad.

00:23:51.090 --> 00:23:55.929
It looks like Belch might be goner, possibly
also Victor.

00:23:55.929 --> 00:23:59.210
We'll see if there end up being any deleted
scenes when the Blu-Ray comes out.

00:23:59.210 --> 00:24:04.460
Moving on, the mural next to the meat place
that Mike works at is constantly changing.

00:24:04.460 --> 00:24:06.279
It starts off innocent enough.

00:24:06.279 --> 00:24:10.789
Then after the kids steal from the drug store,
I noticed it depicting something called "The

00:24:10.789 --> 00:24:13.509
Brutal Battle", which features a dead person.

00:24:13.509 --> 00:24:18.059
Then at some point Pennywise ends up in mural
artwork as well.

00:24:18.059 --> 00:24:22.080
Perhaps the biggest thing I'm looking forward
to in the sequel is the possible inclusion

00:24:22.080 --> 00:24:24.200
of the flood that overruns Derry.

00:24:24.200 --> 00:24:29.460
As a reminder, this happens after the Standpipe
explodes when the remainder of the Losers

00:24:29.460 --> 00:24:30.940
Club defeat IT as adults.

00:24:30.940 --> 00:24:36.110
I didn't catch this the first time around,
because I always imagined The Standpipe to

00:24:36.110 --> 00:24:41.489
be an actual pipe that ruptures, but as it
turns out it's actually a full on building

00:24:41.489 --> 00:24:43.789
and there are a lot of references to it.

00:24:43.789 --> 00:24:49.450
Upon first meeting Ben, he's carrying a school
project which is a model of The Standpipe.

00:24:49.450 --> 00:24:54.450
He ends up dropping it, causing it to pop
off the ground, just like it presumably will

00:24:54.450 --> 00:24:55.450
in the next movie.

00:24:55.450 --> 00:25:00.960
The postcard he buys for Beverly contains
a picture of The Standpipe.

00:25:00.960 --> 00:25:05.850
When he first exits the library he cuts through
Memorial Park, where The Standpipe is supposed

00:25:05.850 --> 00:25:07.239
to be located.

00:25:07.239 --> 00:25:10.239
It’s also somewhat near Beverly's apartment.

00:25:10.239 --> 00:25:14.639
A shot of the Standpipe ends up being used
as a transition before a scene taking place

00:25:14.639 --> 00:25:16.000
at her home.

00:25:16.000 --> 00:25:20.369
And finally, I think that the final battle
with Pennywise at the end of the movie is

00:25:20.369 --> 00:25:23.129
supposed to be located inside The Standpipe.

00:25:23.129 --> 00:25:27.840
When they look up at the giant tower of floating
kids, the shape of the structure that they’re

00:25:27.840 --> 00:25:33.100
in looks to be the same shape as the outside
of The Standpipe, and if it is going to burst,

00:25:33.100 --> 00:25:36.789
it would make sense that the pressure would
start building from directly below.

00:25:36.789 --> 00:25:42.049
And last, but maybe most importantly of all,
Richie's T-shirt in the final scene is a Bike

00:25:42.049 --> 00:25:44.269
and Cycle Shop graphic tee.

00:25:44.269 --> 00:25:49.300
Aside from that being the store that Bill
originally buys his bike, Silver, from in

00:25:49.300 --> 00:25:53.039
the book, I was able to make one other connection.

00:25:53.039 --> 00:25:57.950
The only other Cycling shirt I noticed in
the movie was Georgie's in the very opening

00:25:57.950 --> 00:26:01.539
scene, before he even puts on the raincoat.

00:26:01.539 --> 00:26:04.539
Maybe the word "cycle", takes on a second
meaning here.

00:26:04.539 --> 00:26:10.799
Derry is constantly stuck in a "cycle" of
Pennywise re-emerging every 27 years.

00:26:10.799 --> 00:26:15.679
And this time that cycle begins with the murder
of Georgie and effectively ends when Richie

00:26:15.679 --> 00:26:19.139
has the bravery to stand up and attack Pennywise.

00:26:19.139 --> 00:26:24.619
But like all cycles, the events that make
it up, the spokes of the metaphorical wheel,

00:26:24.619 --> 00:26:27.480
will come around again in Chapter 2.

00:26:27.480 --> 00:26:32.009
I know this video was a little on the long
side, hopefully you found it to be a longy

00:26:32.009 --> 00:26:33.309
but a goody.

00:26:33.309 --> 00:26:36.570
Just like my...

00:26:36.570 --> 00:26:40.769
Last episode of Al Dente Creepypasta, which
you can check out right here.

00:26:40.769 --> 00:26:44.279
Or if you're interested in more Things You
Missed, have a look at this playlist.

00:26:44.279 --> 00:26:45.433
I've got myself a little cycle of my own going
on right now, it's the cycle of new horrors

00:26:45.433 --> 00:26:47.750
every Wednesday and Saturday in October, so
remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new

00:26:47.750 --> 00:26:54.450
horrors every week, ring that death-bell for
notifications and I'll see you in the next

00:26:54.450 --> 00:26:55.450
one.

00:26:55.450 --> 00:26:55.454
Assuming we both survive.

